From 2c96f8d3a4de74649857c4a36758ad62fc309f7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:11:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: judge each monster on its own in borg_flow_kill()

borg_flow_kill() walks the monster list to choose monsters to hunt.
Two pieces of per-monster state were set up once, before the loop:

- skip_monster was never cleared, so once one monster was skipped (for
  example a melee-only monster two grids away), every later monster in
  the list was skipped too.  With such a monster noted first, the borg
  hunted nothing at all, even with another monster in plain view.

- hall_walls, which should count the walls around a pack (GROUP_AI)
  monster, kept counting on from the borg's own surroundings, and the
  "fewer than four walls" test ran inside the counting loop.  The count
  starts at five or more whenever the test is reached, so the test never
  fired and the borg left its corridor to chase pack monsters standing
  in open rooms, which the comment says it should avoid.

Clear skip_monster for each monster, start the wall count at zero for
each monster checked, and test the count once all nine grids are
counted.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#98.

(cherry picked from commit 69862d0f5e2a860d63281df9157d77951875adf3)
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c | 19 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
index 53e26ab0d..3d4439da6 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
@@ -1733,6 +1733,9 @@ bool borg_flow_kill(bool viewable, int nearness)
         int        y9   = kill->pos.y;
         int        ax, ay, d;
 
+        /* Each monster starts with a clean slate */
+        skip_monster = false;
+
         /* Skip dead monsters */
         if (!kill->r_idx)
             continue;
@@ -1812,6 +1815,7 @@ bool borg_flow_kill(bool viewable, int nearness)
         /* Avoid getting surrounded */
         if (borg_in_hall && (rf_has(r_info[kill->r_idx].flags, RF_GROUP_AI))) {
             /* check to see if monster is in a hall, */
+            hall_walls = 0;
             for (hall_x = -1; hall_x <= 1; hall_x++) {
                 for (hall_y = -1; hall_y <= 1; hall_y++) {
                     if (!square_in_bounds_fully(
@@ -1847,15 +1851,16 @@ bool borg_flow_kill(bool viewable, int nearness)
                      * of the room.  This would be dangerous for
                      * him as well.
                      */
-                    /* add 'em up */
-                    if (hall_walls < 4) {
-                        /* This monster is not in a hallway.
-                         * It may not be safe to fight.
-                         */
-                        skip_monster = true;
-                    }
                 }
             }
+
+            /* add 'em up */
+            if (hall_walls < 4) {
+                /* This monster is not in a hallway.
+                 * It may not be safe to fight.
+                 */
+                skip_monster = true;
+            }
         }
 
         /* Skip this one if it is just 2 grids from me and it can attack me as
